From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:25:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: report when VRR page flips are scanned out

With VRR the raster stops at the end of the front porch after each scanout
and waits for a flip. Vblank timestamps assume a blanking interval of the
mode's length, so they are too early by as long as the wait lasted, and flip
events carried them: on a 240 Hz panel at about 60 fps, about 11 ms early, and
about 16.6 ms early for flips arriving during the scanout, whose events are
sent just before their vblank is handled.

A flip kicked off during the wait restarts the raster right away, so report
the kick time plus the rest of the blanking interval (from the start of vsync
to the first active line). Measured against the raster position: the first
active line follows nv_drm_atomic_commit() by 512-554 us, of which 456 us is
that part of the interval. A flip kicked off during the scanout happens at the
next vblank without a wait, so hold its event until that vblank is handled, as
at a fixed refresh rate.

Scanouts forced by the panel's minimum refresh rate aren't known here, but a
flip kicked off during one doesn't restart the raster, so its event arrives late:
measured within 275 us of the commit for flips that did, from 1.3 ms for those
that didn't. Hold an event that took over 500 us until the next vblank too. A
flip kicked off in the last 500 us of a forced scanout is still reported up to
about that much too early.

Flips NVKMS hasn't reported VRR active for keep the previous behaviour, as do
all flips with vrr_flip_timestamps=0, which can be changed at runtime. Tearing
flips are unchanged. This only corrects flip events: vblank timestamps from
CRTC_GET_SEQUENCE and WAIT_VBLANK stay early under VRR, since correcting them
would mean moving the RG semaphore interrupt past the front porch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c      | 106 ++++++++++++++----
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h      |  31 +++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-linux.c     |   6 +
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c   |  30 ++++-
 .../nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.c      |   1 +
 .../nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.h      |   2 +
 6 files changed, 153 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 8d393db3..7e898d78 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -3308,13 +3308,30 @@ failed:
  * hasn't been handled yet, hold the event until it is.
  *
  * Flips that may happen later than that are left without a submit time and
- * reported at the current vblank like before: tearing flips, flips waiting
- * on an unsignaled acquire fence, and flips with VRR enabled (see
- * nv_drm_crtc_set_vblank_duration()).
+ * reported at the current vblank like before: tearing flips and flips waiting
+ * on an unsignaled acquire fence.
+ *
+ * With VRR, the raster stops at the end of the front porch after each scanout
+ * and waits for a flip. A vblank timestamp assumes a blanking interval of the
+ * mode's length, so while the raster waits it is too early by as long as the
+ * wait lasted. A flip that arrives during the wait restarts the raster right
+ * away, so its first active line is the time the flip was kicked off plus the
+ * rest of the blanking interval. A flip that arrives during the scanout
+ * happens at the next vblank without a wait, and is reported at that vblank
+ * like at a fixed refresh rate. So is a flip whose event took longer than
+ * NV_DRM_VRR_FLIP_RESTART_EVENT_NS: it didn't restart the raster, so it arrived
+ * during a scanout the panel's minimum refresh rate forced without a flip,
+ * which aren't known here otherwise.
  */
 
 #define NV_DRM_PENDING_FLIP_EVENTS_TIMEOUT_MS 50
 
+/*
+ * The event of a flip that restarted the raster arrives within about 300 us of
+ * the kick; one latched at the end of a scanout usually takes milliseconds.
+ */
+#define NV_DRM_VRR_FLIP_RESTART_EVENT_NS 500000ULL
+
 static void __nv_drm_crtc_send_flip_event_at(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
                                              struct drm_pending_vblank_event *e,
                                              u64 count, NvU64 time)
@@ -3340,6 +3357,8 @@ static void __nv_drm_crtc_send_flip_events_at(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
 {
     struct nv_drm_flip *nv_deferred_flip, *nv_next_deferred_flip;
 
+    nv_crtc->last_flip_first_active = time;
+
     if (nv_flip->event != NULL) {
         __nv_drm_crtc_send_flip_event_at(&nv_crtc->base, nv_flip->event,
                                          count, time);
@@ -3485,6 +3504,41 @@ static void __nv_drm_crtc_process_pending_flip_events(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crt
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * Find when a VRR flip is scanned out, see the comment above
+ * __nv_drm_crtc_send_flip_event_at(). Returns false if the flip happens at a
+ * vblank that hasn't been handled yet. Called with dev->event_lock and
+ * dev->vblank_time_lock held.
+ */
+static bool __nv_drm_crtc_find_vrr_flip_time(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
+                                             const struct nv_drm_flip *nv_flip,
+                                             u64 *count, NvU64 *time)
+{
+    NvU64 kick_time = READ_ONCE(nv_flip->kick_time);
+
+    if (nv_crtc->vblank_history_len > 0 &&
+        __nv_drm_crtc_find_flip_vblank(nv_crtc, nv_flip, count, time)) {
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    /* The event can be handled before applyModeSetConfig() returns */
+    if (kick_time == 0 || kick_time > nv_flip->event_time) {
+        kick_time = nv_flip->event_time;
+    }
+
+    /* A scanout is still running: wait for its vblank */
+    if (kick_time < nv_crtc->last_flip_first_active +
+                    nv_crtc->vblank_active_ns ||
+        nv_flip->event_time - kick_time > NV_DRM_VRR_FLIP_RESTART_EVENT_NS) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    *count = drm_crtc_vblank_count(&nv_crtc->base);
+    *time = kick_time + nv_crtc->vblank_restart_to_active_ns;
+
+    return true;
+}
+
 /*
  * Called with dev->event_lock held, after nv_flip has been dequeued from the
  * flip list. Returns false if the caller should send the flip's events
@@ -3511,13 +3565,26 @@ bool nv_drm_crtc_handle_flip_events(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
     nv_flip->event_time = event_time;
 
     spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->vblank_time_lock, irqflags);
-    usable = nv_crtc->vblank_intr_fired &&
-             nv_crtc->vblank_history_len > 0 &&
-             nv_crtc->vblank_duration_ns != 0 &&
-             READ_ONCE(nv_flip->submit_time) != 0;
-    if (usable) {
-        found = __nv_drm_crtc_find_flip_vblank(nv_crtc, nv_flip,
-                                               &count, &time);
+    if (nv_flip->vrr) {
+        /* Flips waiting on an acquire fence happened about now */
+        if (READ_ONCE(nv_flip->submit_time) == 0) {
+            WRITE_ONCE(nv_flip->submit_time, event_time);
+        }
+        usable = nv_crtc->vblank_duration_ns != 0 &&
+                 nv_crtc->vblank_active_ns != 0;
+        if (usable) {
+            found = __nv_drm_crtc_find_vrr_flip_time(nv_crtc, nv_flip,
+                                                     &count, &time);
+        }
+    } else {
+        usable = nv_crtc->vblank_intr_fired &&
+                 nv_crtc->vblank_history_len > 0 &&
+                 nv_crtc->vblank_duration_ns != 0 &&
+                 READ_ONCE(nv_flip->submit_time) != 0;
+        if (usable) {
+            found = __nv_drm_crtc_find_flip_vblank(nv_crtc, nv_flip,
+                                                   &count, &time);
+        }
     }
     spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->vblank_time_lock, irqflags);
 
@@ -3636,7 +3703,7 @@ void nv_drm_crtc_set_vblank_duration(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
     struct drm_device *dev = nv_crtc->base.dev;
     const struct drm_display_mode *mode = &crtc_state->adjusted_mode;
     unsigned long irqflags;
-    NvU64 duration = 0, period = 0;
+    NvU64 duration = 0, period = 0, active = 0, restart_to_active = 0;
 
     if (mode->clock > 0 && mode->vtotal > mode->vdisplay) {
         /* mode->clock is in kHz */
@@ -3644,22 +3711,17 @@ void nv_drm_crtc_set_vblank_duration(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
                            mode->htotal * 1000000ULL, mode->clock);
         period = div_u64((u64)mode->vtotal * mode->htotal * 1000000ULL,
                          mode->clock);
+        active = div_u64((u64)mode->vdisplay * mode->htotal * 1000000ULL,
+                         mode->clock);
+        restart_to_active = div_u64((u64)(mode->vtotal - mode->vsync_start) *
+                                    mode->htotal * 1000000ULL, mode->clock);
     }
 
-#if defined(NV_DRM_CRTC_STATE_HAS_VRR_ENABLED)
-    /*
-     * With VRR the blanking interval stretches until a flip arrives, so the
-     * mode's vblank length doesn't tell when the vblank a flip ended started.
-     * A zero duration makes flip events use the current vblank instead.
-     */
-    if (crtc_state->vrr_enabled) {
-        duration = 0;
-    }
-#endif
-
     spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->vblank_time_lock, irqflags);
     nv_crtc->vblank_duration_ns = duration;
     nv_crtc->vblank_period_ns = period;
+    nv_crtc->vblank_active_ns = active;
+    nv_crtc->vblank_restart_to_active_ns = restart_to_active;
     spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->vblank_time_lock, irqflags);
 }
 
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
index c15ec1be..2306362a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
@@ -78,6 +78,21 @@ struct nv_drm_crtc {
      */
     NvU64 vblank_period_ns;
 
+    /*
+     * With VRR the raster waits at the end of the front porch until a flip
+     * arrives, see nv_drm_crtc_handle_flip_events(). These are the length of
+     * the active scanout, and the time from the end of that wait to the first
+     * active line. Protected by dev->vblank_time_lock.
+     */
+    NvU64 vblank_active_ns;
+    NvU64 vblank_restart_to_active_ns;
+
+    /*
+     * First active line of the last flip whose event was sent, and with it
+     * when its scanout ends. Protected by dev->event_lock.
+     */
+    NvU64 last_flip_first_active;
+
     /*
      * Flips whose completion event arrived before the vblank they happened
      * at was handled; their DRM events are sent from the vblank callback.
@@ -99,6 +114,13 @@ struct nv_drm_crtc {
      */
     bool vblank_intr_fired;
 
+    /*
+     * NVKMS reported VRR active for a flip on this CRTC, and the
+     * VRR_ENABLED property has stayed set since. Only used from commits,
+     * which the CRTC's modeset lock serializes.
+     */
+    bool vrr_active;
+
     /**
      * @flip_list:
      *
@@ -216,6 +238,15 @@ struct nv_drm_flip {
      * flip happened before this. Protected by &drm_device.event_lock.
      */
     NvU64 event_time;
+
+    /*
+     * @vrr:
+     *
+     * The raster may be waiting for this flip, so the vblank timestamps
+     * don't tell when it is scanned out. See
+     * nv_drm_crtc_handle_flip_events().
+     */
+    bool vrr;
 };
 
 struct nv_drm_crtc_state {
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-linux.c
index ebc73ffa..b5b63739 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-linux.c
@@ -67,6 +67,12 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(
     "the display scaler (1 = enable (default), 0 = disable)");
 module_param_named(scaling_mode, nv_drm_scaling_mode_module_param, bool, 0444);
 
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(
+    vrr_flip_timestamps,
+    "Report when VRR page flips are scanned out instead of the last vblank "
+    "(1 = enable (default), 0 = disable)");
+module_param_named(vrr_flip_timestamps, nv_drm_vrr_flip_timestamps_module_param, bool, 0644);
+
 #endif /* NV_DRM_AVAILABLE */
 
 /*************************************************************************
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index 27078860..745bd4a4 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -420,6 +420,15 @@ static bool __nv_drm_crtc_state_async_flip(const struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_sta
 #endif
 }
 
+static bool __nv_drm_crtc_state_vrr_enabled(const struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state)
+{
+#if defined(NV_DRM_CRTC_STATE_HAS_VRR_ENABLED)
+    return crtc_state->vrr_enabled;
+#else
+    return false;
+#endif
+}
+
 /*
  * Whether a plane flipped on crtc waits on an acquire fence that hasn't
  * signaled yet, which may delay the flip past the next vblank.
@@ -527,10 +536,17 @@ nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(struct drm_device *dev,
                  * Tearing flips happen right away rather than at a vblank,
                  * and flips waiting on an acquire fence may happen vblanks
                  * later; leave their submit time unset so their events are
-                 * reported at the vblank they arrive at.
+                 * reported at the vblank they arrive at. So do flips with
+                 * VRR enabled that NVKMS hasn't reported VRR active for yet.
                  */
                 nv_new_crtc_state->nv_flip->submit_time = 0;
+                nv_new_crtc_state->nv_flip->vrr =
+                    nv_drm_vrr_flip_timestamps_module_param &&
+                    nv_crtc->vrr_active &&
+                    !__nv_drm_crtc_state_async_flip(new_crtc_state);
                 if (!__nv_drm_crtc_state_async_flip(new_crtc_state) &&
+                    (nv_new_crtc_state->nv_flip->vrr ||
+                     !__nv_drm_crtc_state_vrr_enabled(new_crtc_state)) &&
                     !__nv_drm_crtc_has_unsignaled_in_fence(state, crtc) &&
                     num_submitted_flips < ARRAY_SIZE(submitted_flips)) {
                     submitted_crtcs[num_submitted_flips] = nv_crtc;
@@ -617,9 +633,21 @@ nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(struct drm_device *dev,
 
     if (commit && nv_drm_vblank_module_param) {
         for_each_oldnew_crtc_in_state(state, crtc, old_crtc_state, new_crtc_state, i) {
+            struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc = to_nv_crtc(crtc);
+
             if (old_crtc_state->active && !new_crtc_state->active) {
                 drm_crtc_vblank_off(crtc);
             }
+
+            /*
+             * NVKMS reports no VRR for flips that only update the cursor, so
+             * only VRR_ENABLED turns this off.
+             */
+            if (!__nv_drm_crtc_state_vrr_enabled(new_crtc_state)) {
+                nv_crtc->vrr_active = false;
+            } else if (reply_config.vrrFlip) {
+                nv_crtc->vrr_active = true;
+            }
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.c
index 5a2a04cc..c375d84a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.c
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ bool nv_drm_vblank_module_param = true;
 bool nv_drm_color_pipeline_module_param = true;
 bool nv_drm_deadline_boost_module_param = true;
 bool nv_drm_scaling_mode_module_param = true;
+bool nv_drm_vrr_flip_timestamps_module_param = true;
 
 void *nv_drm_calloc(size_t nmemb, size_t size)
 {
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.h
index 40d11b08..ab5b0209 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-os-interface.h
@@ -74,6 +74,8 @@ extern bool nv_drm_color_pipeline_module_param;
 extern bool nv_drm_deadline_boost_module_param;
 /* Set to true when connectors get the "scaling mode" and underscan properties. */
 extern bool nv_drm_scaling_mode_module_param;
+/* Set to true when VRR flip events report when the flip is scanned out. */
+extern bool nv_drm_vrr_flip_timestamps_module_param;
 
 void *nv_drm_calloc(size_t nmemb, size_t size);
 
